When the switch $S$ is closed, the common potential across the two capacitors becomes $V$. so charge on isolated plates remains same.
$$
\begin{array}{lr}
\therefore \quad C_{0} V_{0}=\left(C_{0}+C\right)V \\
\Rightarrow \quad C V=C_{0} V_{0}-C_{0} V \\
\Rightarrow \quad C=\frac{C_{0}\left(V_{0}-V\right)}{V}
\end{array}
$$
